{"conversation_id":"1b706ff2-93eb-4bd9-9441-e85d96a411d0","status":"SUCCESS","response":"All fixes and acceptance requirements for J7 fix round 2 have been completed and committed per finding.\n\n### 1. Summary of Changes\n\n- **Acquisition cleanup ([udp.jolt](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt#L109-L164), [native.clj](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/build/tools/jolt/stdlib/jolt/socket/native.clj#L511-L547))**:\n  - Wrapped `alloc-sockaddr` with an immediate `try ... (catch Throwable t (ffi/free sa) (throw t))` around `int-cell` (freeing the 128-byte `sockaddr_storage` on length-cell allocation failure).\n  - Wrapped `make-sockaddr` with an immediate `try ... (catch Throwable t (ffi/free sa) (throw t))` around `(ffi/string-\u003eptr (str ip))` (freeing the 16/28-byte `sockaddr` on address-string allocation failure).\n  - Hooked stdlib `native/alloc-sockaddr` and `native/make-sockaddr` via `alter-var-root` and directly in `jolt.socket.native` so all direct and re-def call sites are exception-safe.\n  - Added probe legs tracking allocations in [jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj#L151-L226), confirming 0 unreleased bytes on length-cell failure and address-string failure.\n  - **Commit**: [`8668198f`](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/collab/jolt/j7-fix2.findings.md#L18-L26) `fix(udp): wrap helper acquisitions with exception-safe cleanup (P2)`\n\n- **Receive-error classification ([udp.jolt](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt#L348-L368))**:\n  - Per Linux `udp(7)`, asynchronous errors from earlier datagrams (`ECONNREFUSED` 111, `ECONNRESET` 104, `EMSGSIZE`) are not descriptor-fatal: delivered as instance diagnostics with `:kind :receive-error` while keeping the seam open and writable/readable across turns.\n  - Seam closes once ONLY on genuine descriptor errors (`EBADF`, `ENOTSOCK`, `EPIPE`). `EINTR` remains recoverable, would-block remains silent.\n  - Added probe legs in [jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.clj#L307-L388) verifying injected `ECONNREFUSED` leaves seam open and diagnostic observable with subsequent packet delivery, and injected `EBADF` closes descriptor once with idempotent closure.\n  - **Commit**: [`ebbd0199`](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/collab/jolt/j7-fix2.findings.md#L28-L41) `fix(udp): classify genuine descriptor errors vs asynchronous receive errors (P2)`\n\n- **Evidence \u0026 Findings Report ([j7-fix2.findings.md](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/collab/jolt/j7-fix2.findings.md))**:\n  - Full findings and acceptance outputs recorded in [collab/jolt/j7-fix2.findings.md](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/collab/jolt/j7-fix2.findings.md).\n  - **Commit**: [`a7c82518`](file:///home/sto/ci/dw-j7/collab/jolt/j7-fix2.findings.md) `docs(collab): J7 fix round 2 findings and acceptance evidence`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Acceptance Verification\n\n| Check | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Failure-injection probe | `bb probe:jolt-udp-failures` | **83/83 passed, 0 failed** (exit 0) |\n| Retained UDP probe | `bb probe:jolt-udp` | **37/37 passed, 0 failed** (exit 0) |\n| Solo DHT smoke on Jolt | `printf '(+ 1 2)\\n' \\| \"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-yin-repl --no-state --index-store dht:/tmp/...` | **Boots and evaluates `(+ 1 2)` =\u003e 3** (exit 0) |\n| JVM test suites | `java -cp \"$CP\" clojure.main -m cognitect.test-runner -n dao.stream.udp-test -n dao.stream.udp-raw-test -n dao.stream.datagram-test` | **37 tests, 185 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (exit 0) |\n| Jolt test runner | `\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.stream.udp-test dao.stream.udp-raw-test dao.stream.datagram-test` | **37 tests, 185 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (exit 0) |\n| Reviewer injection script | `\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt build/j7-review/native-injection.clj` | **35 contract assertions passed** (exit 0) |\n","duration_seconds":1104.933825499,"num_t